  "note": [
    "How much potency each job lands per second. The one part of the damage estimate that is not",
    "arithmetic on the stats.",
    "",
    "potencyPerSecond comes from a rotation simulator's UNBUFFED expected potency per second, which is",
    "exactly the quantity the model multiplies damage per 100 potency by. The sims' dps column was NOT",
    "used to calibrate: it is buffed and the buffs are job-specific, so dividing it back out would",
    "reintroduce a per-job guess to remove a per-job guess.",
    "",
    "  potencyPerSecond  what the sim reports for a known set",
    "  referenceGcd      that set's recast, so the figure can be moved to another one",
    "  gcdShare          how much of the potency is bound to the global cooldown. The only estimate",
    "                    left, and deliberately so: it decides how the number moves with a speed stat,",
    "                    not what the number is.",
    "  calibrated        true once potencyPerSecond came from a sim",
    "",
    "Fifteen jobs are calibrated. Bard and machinist have no sim yet and carry the estimate scaled by",
    "the dancer's correction \u2014 same category, one measurement, and the dancer came in 18% under. The",
    "four casters have no measured sibling and stay as they were.",
    "",
    "trait and attackPowerMultiplier are measured, one Etro set per category:",
